BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Durham Writers Group
UID:event_315995163@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260822T021031Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260825T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260825T213000
SUMMARY:*IN-PERSON* SF/F Group
DESCRIPTION:Durham Writers Group\nWe will be at the Moon House at 3039 Uni
 versity Dr. in Durham. This venue does not serve food or drink\, but feel 
 free to bring your own. There is a kitchenette for our use\, but be sure t
 o clean up afterwards. The space might be a little cozy\; please consider 
 masking or staying home if you have a respiratory ailment.\n\nThis sub-gro
 up focuses on Speculative Fiction\, including Science Fiction\, Fantasy an
 d Horror. If you have anything that falls under that category — be it sh
 ort story\, poem\, novel-in-progress or screenplay — then come! We'd lov
 e to hear from you.\n\nOur format allows each reader 15 minutes to present
  their work aloud\, followed by approximately 20 minutes of feedback from 
 the other attendees. To ensure fairness\, each attendee is limited to 1 mi
 nute of Initial Feedback time. During that period\, the author remains sil
 ent. Next\, we have a 5 minute Free-For-All discussion about the work -- t
 hen the author may speak. (We usually get through three readers.)\n\nThoug
 h not required\, in order to receive more in-depth feed-back\, readers may
  post their work in advance on our Google Group:\nhttps://groups.google.co
 m/d/forum/durham-sff-writers-group\n\nWe ask that participants keep their 
 comments constructive and respectful\, focusing on what works or doesn't w
 ork in the piece.\n\nWe also ask that readers provide a warning\, both on 
 the Google Group and during the meeting\, if their story features content 
 that some readers might find upsetting. This includes descriptions of viol
 ence or sexual content.\n\nReaders are:\n• Tricia\n• Rob L\n• Milbre
 \n\nBackup Readers are:\n• James\n• Dan\n• Rob S\n\nDeep Backup:\n
 • Ada\n\n***\n\n***We meet every Tuesday at the same time\, but alternat
 e between In-Person*** ***and on Zoom. Members may attend both formats\, i
 f desired\, but readers will be listed separately under the In-Person or Z
 oom weeks.***
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/dwg-writers/events/315995163/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260805T224442Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260805T224442Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Durham Writers Group
UID:event_316091486@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260822T021031Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260901T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260901T213000
SUMMARY:*VIRTUAL* SF/F Group
DESCRIPTION:Durham Writers Group\n**Zoom Info Below Description**\n\nThis 
 sub-group focuses on Science Fiction and Fantasy\, so if you have anything
  that falls under that category — be it short story\, poem\, novel-in-pr
 ogress or screenplay — then come! We'd love to hear from you.\n\nOur for
 mat allows each reader 15 minutes to present their work... followed by app
 roximately 20 minutes of feedback from the other attendees. To ensure a fa
 ir opportunity to respond\, each attendee is limited to 1 minute of feedba
 ck time. (We usually get through three readers.)\n\nIf a reader elects to 
 post their work in advance (NOT a requirement!)\, members will be able to 
 access that work at our Google Group:\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/forum/d
 urham-sff-writers-group\n\nWe ask all members to provide a warning\, both 
 on the Google Group and during the meeting\, if their story features conte
 nt that some readers might find upsetting. This includes descriptions of s
 exual violence.\n\nReaders are:\n• Naveed\n• Charlie\n• Dara\n\nBack
 up Readers are:\n• Lucy\n• Maggie\n• Sigma\n\nDeep Backup:\nFraser\n
 \n***\n\n***We meet every Tuesday at the same time\, but alternate between
  meeting In-Person and on Zoom. Members may attend both formats\, if desir
 ed\, but readers will be listed separately under the In-Person or Zoom wee
 ks.***\n\n> Enabled for both audio and video. Users can choose what to sha
 re.\n> Users can share their screen/application\, which could be good for 
 reading along.\n> There is a shareable whiteboard.\n> Users can annotate t
 he screen.\n> You can set up polls (host only?).\n\nJoin Zoom Meeting\n[ht
 tps://us02web.zoom.us/j/81691827858?pwd=klZQya0UmbCjYHPnjbiTV3uIPS5ulg.1](
 https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fus02web.zoom.us%2Fj%2F816918278
 58%3Fpwd%3DklZQya0UmbCjYHPnjbiTV3uIPS5ulg.1&sa=D&source=calendar&ust=17779
 11660000000&usg=AOvVaw0K3t6Pl7xCXBU6EwFwranp)\n\nMeeting ID: 816 9182 7858
 \nPasscode: 004234\n\nDial by your location\n+13017158592\,\,81691827858#\
 ,\,\,\,\\*004234# US (Washington DC)\n\n+13052241968\,\,81691827858#\,\,\,
 \,\\*004234# US\n\nJoin by SIP\n• [81691827858@zoomcrc.com](mailto:81691
 827858@zoomcrc.com)\n\nJoin by H.323\n162.255.36.11 (US East)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/dwg-writers/events/316091486/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260812T225119Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260812T225119Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
